# Claude Code Configuration

This file provides Claude Code with comprehensive workflow instructions for creative writing using Novel-OS.

## Novel-OS (Creative Writing System)

Novel-OS is a structured AI-assisted novel writing system that transforms AI writing agents into productive creative partners.

### Novel-OS Structure
```
~/.novel-os/
├── standards/                  # Writing standards and style guides
│   ├── writing-style.md        # General writing style guide
│   ├── narrative-techniques.md # Narrative technique guidelines
│   └── genre-guides/           # Genre-specific writing guides
│       ├── literary-fiction.md
│       ├── mystery-thriller.md
│       └── fantasy-sci-fi.md
└── instructions/               # Novel-OS workflow instructions
    └── core/                   # Core writing workflow processes
        ├── plan-novel.md       # Novel planning and setup
        ├── create-outline.md   # Chapter/scene outline creation
        ├── write-scenes.md     # Scene writing workflows
        ├── write-scene.md      # Individual scene writing
        └── analyze-manuscript.md # Manuscript analysis
```

### Novel-OS Commands

Users can invoke Novel-OS workflows directly using these commands:

```
/plan-novel          → Execute novel planning workflow
/create-outline      → Create detailed chapter/scene outlines
/write-scenes        → Begin scene writing with guided workflows
/analyze-manuscript  → Analyze existing manuscript content
```

### Command Processing
When a user types a Novel-OS command (e.g., `/plan-novel`):

1. **Read the command file** from `~/.claude/commands/[command-name].md`
2. **Execute the corresponding workflow** from `~/.novel-os/instructions/core/[command-name].md`
3. **Apply writing standards** from `~/.novel-os/standards/` as needed
4. **Follow the complete workflow** as defined in the instruction files

### Command Examples
```
User types: /plan-novel
→ Read: ~/.claude/commands/plan-novel.md
→ Execute: ~/.novel-os/instructions/core/plan-novel.md

User types: /create-outline
→ Read: ~/.claude/commands/create-outline.md  
→ Execute: ~/.novel-os/instructions/core/create-outline.md

User types: /write-scenes
→ Read: ~/.claude/commands/write-scenes.md
→ Execute: ~/.novel-os/instructions/core/write-scenes.md

User types: /analyze-manuscript
→ Read: ~/.claude/commands/analyze-manuscript.md
→ Execute: ~/.novel-os/instructions/core/analyze-manuscript.md
```

